----------------------------------------------------------------------
SCOPE / PARITY
----------------------------------------------------------------------
The web <InlineCallout> is a PURE presentational component: (variant, icon?, children, action?) ->
an inline element, with NO fetch / cache / promise. It therefore has NO loading/error/stale/offline
data branch — there is nothing to fetch, fail, age, or lose connectivity to. Inventing such chrome
would fabricate states the source does not have, so this surface reproduces ONLY the source's REAL
branches (exactly as the sibling presentational primitives Delta(0081), MetricCard(0095),
BatteryDelta(0077) did). Real branches reproduced:
  • 4 severity variants: info / success / warning / danger
  • 3 wrapper interactions: status (<div role="status">) / link (<a href>) / button (<button onClick>),
    href preferred over onClick (web "passing both prefers href")
  • optional leading icon (SF Symbol) + optional trailing action label + chevron
  • body colour split: info/success -> --text-secondary; warning/danger -> tinted (web amber-200/85 /
    rose-200/85); icon + trailing -> variant tint (web text-{c}-300)
Bound through the P1/S8 state-holder (InlineCalloutModel); token-driven chrome (P1/S9); i18n facade
(P1/S10); once-only view.opened diagnostics (P1/S11). No direct HTTP, no Tailwind ports.

